From 0457d471b51dd0da4fbb65d4326fe9eca9c6ed96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 00:58:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 114/115] usb: cdns3: restore full sky1-next USBSSP driver set
 (host-enable hang)

cdnsp-sky1.c alone was insufficient: the host-enable path hangs in
cdns_role_start(HOST) during xHCI bring-up (dyndbg: role 0->1 then wedge).
The regression lives in the cdns core host-enable (core.c/drd.c/host.c/
cdnsp-plat.c), all heavily diverged from the working 7.0.12-sky1-next tree.

Restore the complete sky1-next cdnsp USBSSP driver set (core, drd, host,
cdnsp-plat/gadget/ep0/mem/ring + headers) which is proven on this exact
CIX Sky1 hardware+ACPI (edge boots USB/kbd/mouse/BT). Supersedes the
partial 0112/0113 port work.
